Feature: Scene & Surface Lifecycle Management
  As a platform operator
  I want scene detection, deletion, and export to respect data integrity
  So that approved surfaces aren't silently destroyed, orphans don't pollute the database,
  and individual scenes can be exported for external tools

  Background:
    Given the BIT platform ingests video content and detects scenes with AI
    And scenes contain surfaces that can be approved for ad placement
    And approved surfaces have associated AdSlots and ApprovalItems
    And RenderItems reference both ContentId and SurfaceId

  # ── Re-detect Safety ──

  Scenario: Re-detect is blocked when approved surfaces exist
    Given a content item "v-01" has scene "s-01"
    And scene "s-01" has surface "sf-01" with Status "Approved"
    When I trigger re-detect scenes for "v-01"
    Then the Hangfire job fails with an InvalidOperationException
    And the error message states "Cannot re-detect: 1 approved surface(s) exist. Exclude or reject them first."
    And no scenes or surfaces are deleted
    And the content status is set to "Failed" with the error message

  Scenario: Re-detect succeeds when no approved surfaces exist
    Given a content item "v-01" has scenes with only Candidate/Excluded surfaces
    When I trigger re-detect scenes for "v-01"
    Then existing scenes and surfaces are deleted
    And new scenes and surfaces are created from the fresh detection
    And the pipeline completes successfully

  # ── Content Deletion Cascade ──

  Scenario: Deleting a video cleans up all child entities
    Given a content item "v-01" with scenes, surfaces, ad slots, approvals, and renders
    When I call DELETE /api/content/v-01
    Then the ContentItem is removed
    And all SceneItems with ContentId "v-01" are removed
    And all SurfaceItems belonging to those scenes are removed
    And all AdSlotItems referencing those surfaces are removed
    And all ApprovalItems referencing those ad slots are removed
    And all RenderItems with ContentId "v-01" or those SurfaceIds are removed

  Scenario: Deleting a video with no scenes succeeds cleanly
    Given a content item "v-01" in Staging with no scenes
    When I call DELETE /api/content/v-01
    Then the ContentItem is removed with no errors
    And no orphaned rows remain

  # ── Single Scene Deletion ──

  Scenario: Delete a single scene that has no approved surfaces
    Given scene "s-01" has surfaces all with Status "Candidate" or "Excluded"
    When I call DELETE /api/scenes/s-01
    Then the scene is removed
    And all its surfaces, ad slots, and approvals are removed
    And the response is 200 OK

  Scenario: Delete a single scene blocked by approved surface
    Given scene "s-01" has a surface with Status "Approved"
    When I call DELETE /api/scenes/s-01
    Then the response is 400 Bad Request
    And the error message identifies the approved surface
    And no data is modified

  Scenario: Delete a non-existent scene returns 404
    When I call DELETE /api/scenes/nonexistent
    Then the response is 404 Not Found

  # ── Bulk Scene Deletion ──

  Scenario: Bulk delete all scenes for a video
    Given content "v-01" has 50 scenes, none with approved surfaces
    When I call DELETE /api/content/v-01/scenes
    Then all 50 scenes and their child entities are removed
    And the response is 200 OK with count of deleted scenes

  Scenario: Bulk delete blocked by any approved surface
    Given content "v-01" has 50 scenes, and scene "s-25" has an approved surface
    When I call DELETE /api/content/v-01/scenes
    Then the response is 400 Bad Request
    And the error message identifies which scene has the approved surface
    And no data is modified

  # ── Scene Clip Export ──

  Scenario: Export a scene as a standalone video clip
    Given scene "s-01" has StartFrame 1500 and EndFrame 4500
    And the source video exists at the content's StorageKey path
    When I call GET /api/scenes/s-01/clip
    Then the response is a video/mp4 file
    And the clip contains only frames 1500 through 4500
    And the HTTP response includes Content-Disposition: attachment

  Scenario: Export clip fails when source video is missing
    Given scene "s-01" references a content item whose video file does not exist on disk
    When I call GET /api/scenes/s-01/clip
    Then the response is 404 with error "Source video file not found"

  Scenario: Export clip fails when scene not found
    When I call GET /api/scenes/nonexistent/clip
    Then the response is 404 Not Found

  # ── Frontend Confirmation ──

  Scenario: Re-detect shows confirmation dialog
    Given the user is viewing a completed content item in the IngestionTab
    When the user clicks "Re-detect Scenes"
    Then a confirmation modal appears
    And the modal warns that existing scenes and surfaces will be destroyed
    And the user must click a second time to confirm
    And clicking cancel dismisses the modal without action
